{"id": "EUVD-2026-82211", "enisaUuid": "ee7a4f44-c20d-3323-b3fc-4a8663140275", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/hfi1: Preserve unit 0 on allocation failure\n\nhfi1_free_devdata() assumes that the device was inserted into the unit\ntable and unconditionally erases dd->unit. If xa_alloc_irq() fails, the\nzero-initialized unit remains zero, so full cleanup can remove an\nunrelated device from index 0.\n\nRelease only the rdmavt allocation and return immediately while the unit\ntable has not acquired the device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/852637d3ee56aed8ea3ee8948eda21eca406c051", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d0e5252b8d0345ef494763ca31e3ddd666e02cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0feb29d434e6cc0ebefec4f77be014c85ad751b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3f1e196eb66b8cd3882e373794d6cea46f150a20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ff9d58d34758e9633078b37e8d5289b513ff80e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd4d3ad5f244a867166d1e2da7ece3d82878ec81", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4204f5c0312ba136181a6e148ffa0bfaf95a4cc1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e3809ad8911f5d5581b3f046bd628417bface76"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93103", "GHSA-jjcw-q5gq-x45h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0054c23e-ce17-3597-b011-04ba224e32ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "03b92789e5cfdac66805c1a98f1ec67336199d56 <3f1e196eb66b8cd3882e373794d6cea46f150a20"}, {"id": "01b39aff-80db-381a-97ed-84f45a76c2f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "16b3f865-6ce2-39dc-b8e4-1ef6ba44d187", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "03b92789e5cfdac66805c1a98f1ec67336199d56 <4ff9d58d34758e9633078b37e8d5289b513ff80e"}, {"id": "2d9e6940-6dc6-3e97-bb